          "summary": "Add general-advertising and unsolicited-approach carve-outs to the mutual non-solicitation clause.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] We can live with a mutual, twelve-month non-solicit limited to personnel directly involved in the Services, but we need the standard carve-outs so that general job advertisements, untargeted recruiter searches and hires of people who approach us on their own initiative are not caught. This is our fallback position and keeps the restriction narrow for both parties.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0047",
              "oldText": "without such other party's express written consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld.",
              "newText": "without such other party's express written consent, which shall not be unreasonably withheld. Notwithstanding the foregoing, nothing in this Section shall restrict either party from (a) conducting general solicitations for employment, including general advertisements, job postings and searches by recruiting firms, in each case not specifically directed at the other party's personnel, or (b) employing or engaging any person who responds to such a general solicitation or who approaches such party on his or her own initiative without solicitation."
